      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14244048/assets/d805cc4e6c4b817cc4a00d4cccfca59a8bb89ba49442b01deaed3ec75c2ffc1b.png)\n\nFind the minimum value of the parabola $y=3(x+5)^{2}-6$, sketched above.",
      "worked_solution": "The minimum value of the parabola is the $y$-coordinate of the vertex of the parabola. \n\nRemember that the vertex form of a parabola is\n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k\n$$\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola.\n\nThe given parabola\n\n$$\ny=3(x+5)^{2}-6\n$$\n\nis written in vertex form with $h=-5$ and $k=-6.$ Therefore, the vertex of the parabola is at $(-5,-6),$ and its minimum value is $-6.$",
